     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9000 mg/day of acetaminophen is more than twice the maximum daily dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that's appropriate. It could cause acute liver injury or liver failure in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the dose, such as a protocol or a miscommunication about the intended regimen, please check it with your attending or a clinical pharmacist. The order can go through whatever override process your institution requires.\n\nI can enter a dose within the safe range right now. For example:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4000 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain control, I can also help with adding a non-acetaminophen agent. Tell me which option you want."
